// Cyrus R5: the DELIVERY ORCHESTRATOR. Installs / updates / uninstalls one Cyrus mod (plugin jar + resource pack +
// data packs + world generation + managed plugins + creatures) or one Mod Pack on ONE server, as one transaction-like
// sequence:
//   open -> recover check (a left-over journal refuses) -> preflight (server inventory + conflict engine against what is
//   already there: blocking refuses, warnings are recorded; release bytes verified; Pack Loader config valid) ->
//   [snapshot managed-plugin refs] -> ensure managed plugins (Pack Loader, BetterModel) -> host the pack (immutable URL)
//   -> Pack Loader config -> place jar / data packs / creature models (all through the copy-on-write journal) -> delivery
//   record -> apply ONLY as the semantics require (restart / minecraft:reload / nothing) -> HEALTH CHECK (answers,
//   plugins enabled, no new error lines, data packs loaded, worldgen: really came up) -> BetterModel hand-off (after the
//   restart) -> commit.
// ANY failure after preflight rolls back to the exact previous state: every journaled file (bytes verified), the
// managed-plugin refs (database rows), and, when the server was restarted or reloaded, restarts / reloads it again and
// checks that it came up; why is recorded step by step. Mod Packs reuse the same transaction (their unit installer
// writes through the same journal), so a pack is still one unit.
// OFF unless CYRUS_DELIVERY=1 (and each part behind its existing flag: CYRUS_MANAGED_PLUGINS_REAL,
// CYRUS_DATAPACK_DELIVERY_REAL (+ CYRUS_WORLDGEN), CYRUS_CREATURES, CYRUS_MODPACK_INSTALL_REAL).
