docs/DOCUMENTATION.md:22666:**The flow.** Build request (plan gate kind `model` = top plan, version capability `animatedCreatures` + buildable, the flag) -> the build service's AI writes a RigSpec `assets/creatures/<name>.json` (template form recommended) + plugin code that spawns a silent, invisible vanilla base mob and attaches the model through the BetterModel API (compile-only, on the javac classpath) -> the service validates the spec with the generated validator (bounded repairs, drop-don't-ship) -> the portal re-validates, **compiles** the RigSpec to a Blockbench `.bbmodel` (format 5.0) + skin PNG + baked keyframes, runs the skin quality bar, records a revision + `CyrusProjectAsset` kind `model` -> (worker, flags on) Nxeon ensures the managed **BetterModel 3.5.0** plugin, writes its managed config and `plugins/BetterModel/models/<namespace>_<name>.bbmodel` -> restart: BetterModel builds its own resource pack (`plugins/BetterModel/build.zip`) -> the hand-off normalises it, hosts it by sha1 and adds ONE server-level Pack Loader entry next to each mod's own pack.
docs/DOCUMENTATION.md:22674:- **Pack hand-off** (`lib/cyrus/creature/handoff.ts`): read `build.zip` through the GuestFs, check it (zip check, only `pack.mcmeta`/`pack.png`/`assets/bettermodel/**`, no symlinks/duplicates, 32 MB cap), **re-zip deterministically** (sorted, fixed timestamps) so the same content keeps the same sha1, `publishPack`, upsert one Pack Loader entry (reserved pseudo-namespace `nx_bmodel00`, role `bettermodel`, owner `bettermodel`, `required: false`). Verified: first and second boot normalise to the same pack (sha1 `39acdb7c...ef9e` for the 3 fixtures), a second hand-off is `unchanged`, and the Pack Loader on a real server accepted the resulting `packs.json` next to BetterModel. Not wired into a worker job yet (it must run AFTER the restart that follows a delivery): the owner/next slice decides the trigger (worker step after a restart, or a `/bettermodel reload` + read).
